From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/perf: apple_m1: Match the T8132 (M4) PMU

Register apple,t8132-pmu with the M4 event table, counter mask (0-7) and
63-bit overflow of the T6040 and T8140 entries, named apple_t8132_pmu.

The event placement was measured on M4 Pro (T6040) and A18 Pro (T8140)
cores only. That the T8132 cores count the same events on the same
counters is an inference until the reference loops of "Support the M4
and A18 core PMUs" have been counted on a T8132; the device tree node
stays disabled until then.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 5d76a9df5d3118cfda5c2e7c2d1cb484ed285a80)
(cherry picked from commit 604bdcb838dea32a0ddf461398e5e90bb2f99314)
---
 drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c b/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
index 3042805a77..2d1858093e 100644
--- a/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
@@ -867,6 +867,12 @@ static int m4_pmu_t6040_init(struct arm_pmu *cpu_pmu)
 	return m4_pmu_init(cpu_pmu);
 }
 
+static int m4_pmu_t8132_init(struct arm_pmu *cpu_pmu)
+{
+	cpu_pmu->name = "apple_t8132_pmu";
+	return m4_pmu_init(cpu_pmu);
+}
+
 static int m4_pmu_t8140_init(struct arm_pmu *cpu_pmu)
 {
 	cpu_pmu->name = "apple_t8140_pmu";
@@ -876,6 +882,7 @@ static int m4_pmu_t8140_init(struct arm_pmu *cpu_pmu)
 static const struct of_device_id m1_pmu_of_device_ids[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-pmu",	.data = m4_pmu_t8140_init, },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t6040-pmu",	.data = m4_pmu_t6040_init, },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-pmu",	.data = m4_pmu_t8132_init, },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,avalanche-pmu",	.data = m2_pmu_avalanche_init, },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,blizzard-pmu",	.data = m2_pmu_blizzard_init, },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,icestorm-pmu",	.data = m1_pmu_ice_init, },
